al Behavior\\n\\nMultiple Electron applications terminate during startup.\\n\\nThe logs consistently end with:\\n\\n```text\\n[FATAL:content\\\\browser\\\\gpu\\\\gpu_data_manager_impl_private.cc:415]\\nGPU process isn't usable. Goodbye.\\n```\\n\\nSignal additionally reports repeated GPU process failures before aborting:\\n\\n```text\\nGPU process exited unexpectedly: exit_code=-2147483645\\n```\\n\\nWindows Event Viewer records Application Error (Event ID 1000) with exception code:\\n\\n```\\n0x80000003\\n```\\n\\nThe faulting module is the application executable itself (e.g. `Obsidian.exe`, `Signal.exe`).\\n\\n## Reproduction\\n\\nLaunching Obsidian normally:\\n\\n```powershell\\n& \\\"C:\\\\Users\\\\<user>\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Programs\\\\Obsidian\\\\Obsidian.exe\\\"\\n```\\n\\nResults in:\\n\\n* application exits almost immediately\\n* log ends with `GPU process isn't usable. Goodbye.`\\n\\nThe same behavior is observed with Signal Desktop and Discord.\\n\\n## Startup Flag Testing\\n\\n### `--in-process-gpu`\\n\\nLaunching with:\\n\\n```text\\n--in-process-gpu\\n```\\n\\nchanges the behavior:\\n\\n* the process no longer exits immediately\\n* however, the application window is not rendered correctly (GUI is missing / blank)\\n\\n### Four-flag combination\\n\\nLaunching with:\\n\\n```text\\n--disable-gpu\\n--disable-gpu-compositing\\n--disable-software-rasterizer\\n--in-process-gpu\\n```\\n\\nchanges the behavior further.\\n\\nIn Safe Mode, this combination allows the UI to render instead of immediately terminating.\\n\\nOutside Safe Mode, startup behavior changes, but rendering is still incomplete or absent.\\n\\nThe fact that `--in-process-gpu` consistently changes the failure mode suggests the issue is related to Chromium's GPU process initialization.\\n\\n## Diagnostics Already Performed\\n\\n* Updated AMD driver to latest available version\\n* `sfc /scannow`\\n* Windows Defender scan\\n* Malwarebytes scan\\n* HDR disabled\\n* Safe Mode testing\\n* AMD Radeon Software terminated\\n* DxDiag reports no display or DirectX problems\\n\\nNone of the above resolved the issue.\\n\\nIf there are additional Chromium or Electron logging flags that would help diagnose why the GPU process exits, I would be happy to collect and provide them.\\n\\n### Testcase Gist URL\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Additional Information\\n\\nVisual Studio Code launches normally on the same machine.\\n\\nThis suggests the issue is not a complete Electron failure, but may depend on the Electron/Chromium version or GPU initialization path used by different applications.\",\n  \"form\": \"bug\",\n  \"labels_already_applied\": [\n   \"blocked/need-info ❌\",\n   \"bug :beetle:\",\n   \"platform/windows\"\n  ],\n  \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n  \"opened\": \"2026-07-03T10:57:47Z\"\n },\n \"form_fields\": {\n  \"electron_version\": \"Electron 39.8.3\",\n  \"os\": \"Windows\",\n  \"last_known_working\": null,\n  \"testcase_gist_url\": null\n },\n \"repro\": {\n  \"gist\": false,\n  \"other_repo_link\": false,\n  \"code_blocks\": 6\n },\n \"bot_already\": {\n  \"asked_for_supported_version\": true,\n  \"need_repro_label\": false\n },\n \"issues_linked_by_reporter\": [\n  51761,\n  52098\n ],\n \"component_hints\": [\n  {\n   \"label\": \"component/gpu\",\n   \"matched\": [\n    \"gpu\",\n    \"gpu process\"\n   ],\n   \"in_title\": true\n  }\n ],\n \"redirect_hints\": {\n  \"upstream\": [\n   \"chromium\"\n  ]\n },\n \"similar_candidates\": [\n  {\n   \"number\": 52098,\n   \"opened\": \"2026-06-23\",\n   \"score\": 130.9,\n   \"title\": \"GPU/renderer process crashes with EXCEPTION_BREAKPOINT (0x80000003) on Windows 11 25H2 (build 26200.8655) — sandbox init failure, regression after June 2026 cumulative update\",\n   \"shared_terms\": [\n    \"radeon\",\n    \"exit_code\",\n    \"x80000003\",\n    \"faulting\",\n    \"0x80000003\",\n    \"goodbye.\",\n    \"gpu_data_manager_impl_private.cc\",\n    \"-2147483645\"\n   ],\n   \"already_linked_by_reporter